Effect-record hook 1: the trigger-handler cause channel.

Stage-one collection attributes an event to whatever the stack said was
resolving when the event arrived. That is right whenever one thing resolves at a
time and wrong whenever two do — a trigger that fires during another ability's
resolution is attributed to the ability, not to itself.

This hook adds a static, per-thread pointer that the trigger handler sets while
it runs a trigger, so a collector can ask "whose trigger is this" instead of
inferring it. It also adds AbilityKey.Cause at the Destroyed firing site, where
the ability that caused the destruction is in scope and is currently dropped —
without it a destroy record cannot name what destroyed the permanent.

The pointer is a plain static field rather than a listener interface so the
connector can read it reflectively and keep building against stock Forge.

--- a/forge-game/src/main/java/forge/game/trigger/TriggerHandler.java
